{
  "title": "Account for shell timeout wrappers around agent-submit",
  "description": "The PreToolUse hook unwraps the shell timeout executable but discards its duration.\n\
A command such as timeout 1 agent-submit --title T --body B is currently allowed when the execution tool supplies a 70-minute timeout, even though the shell wrapper terminates it after one second.\n\
This also affects persistent execution sessions because their lifetime does not remove a timeout imposed inside the shell command.\n\
Preserve wrapper duration metadata and reject insufficient shell timeouts around agent-submit, including nested shell and env wrappers.\n\
Add regression coverage for short and sufficient wrapper durations while preserving the existing tool-lifetime checks.\n\
This is a pre-existing command-parsing gap found while implementing Codex persistent-session support; it is separate from identifying the execution tool and its yield semantics.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "pretool-hook",
    "agent-submit",
  ],
